{
  "metadata": {
    "name": "A1 \u00b7 unity output gain, PM-band c_init (eff loop gain 0.75)",
    "description": "Cheap-hypothesis sweep arm: motor_gain 3.0->1.0 with c_init 0.25->0.75, holding the effective loop gain motor_gain*c_init at the baseline's 0.75. Isolates the CLIPPING regime: at motor_gain 3.0 a third of the tanh's range already exceeds the adapter's |u|<=1 clamp, so the body applies a hard discontinuity the HK loop-Jacobian models as smooth. At unity gain the same loop gain arrives without the clip. This is the Playful Machine's own operating convention (Sox cInit 0.7-1.2 at UNITY output gain).",
    "env_target": "microduck",
    "phase_tag": "A1 (first brain)",
    "scaffolds_active": [
      "alpha_stand.onnx via the A2 recovery harness \u2014 drives only while the body is down, with all learning rates zeroed"
    ]
  },
  "version": 1,
  "runtime": {
